with 18 000 police officers guarding the  summit these protesters rode their luck  and tried to grab the attention of the  leaders urging the g7 to do everything  possible to stop the war in ukraine  they're talking about the war the  destruction of the world the climate  catastrophe and we want to show our  protest  inside the castle ukrainian president  zelinski invited to attend fire video  link was asking for more weapons telling  the g7 leaders he wanted the war to be  over before winter for their part the  united states announced it would send  new advanced air defense systems to  ukraine  while g7 leaders discussed increasing  military firepower nato chief yan  stoltenberg in brussels announce a large  expansion of battle-ready troops we will  strengthen our forward defenses  we will enhance our battlegroups in the  eastern part of the alliance  up to brigade levels  we will transform the nato response  force  and increase the number of our high  readiness forces to well over  300 000  such massive numbers making this the  biggest overhaul of nato's deterrent  since the cold war  it is clear that this war has a very  deep impact on international relations  as i said before i see russia's attack  on ukraine as a turning point all  international rules of corporation have  been broken especially that borders  can't be changed by force we as g7 agree  that these will be long lasting effects  and will stay with us a very long time  and influence international relations  for a very long time  it's been a delicate balancing act here  at the castle thousand meters high in  the bavarian alps how to increase  pressure on russia and continue to  support ukraine while making sure that  sanctions won't backfire on g7 economies  developing countries are also paying a  very high price  indonesian president joko widodo invited  as one of the guests to the summit urged  the g7 to find a solution to the food  crisis hitting developing nations as a  result of the war together with u.n  secretary general antonio guterres  leaders discussed ways to lift the  blockade of ukrainian food stocks with  widespread humanitarian disasters  looming and the war in ukraine ongoing  g7 leaders will leave the bavarian alps  with multiple crises unresolved next on  their agenda the nato summit in madrid  later this week step fast on al jazeera  and garmish partnership
 

